╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ share_rz_pre_post_params                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses independent RZ parameters before and after the entangling CZ      │
│                          │ chain (rz_pre_i and rz_post_i for each of the 8 qubits), giving 16 distinct RZ parameters │
│                          │ plus 8 RY parameters = 24 distinct trainable parameters total. Since parameter economy is │
│                          │ heavily rewarded (fewer distinct parameter names always scores higher), we merge the pre- │
│                          │ and post-entanglement RZ rotations on each qubit into a single shared parameter name      │
│                          │ (rz_i). This halves the RZ parameter count from 16 to 8, bringing total distinct          │
│                          │ parameters from 24 down to 16, while still keeping a per-qubit RZ rotation on both sides  │
│                          │ of the entangling layer (now correlated rather than independent), preserving most of the  │
│                          │ circuit's expressive structure and its ability to build entanglement-dependent phase      │
│                          │ structure that helps separate the hardest validation groups. This should improve          │
│                          │ parameter_efficiency and the combined score without sacrificing much accuracy, since the  │
│                          │ model was already at ceiling accuracy (train/val/test ~1.0) and clearly over-parametrized │
│                          │ for the task.                                                                             │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0332                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
│ system_prompt_id         │ None                                                                                      │
│ model_name               │ openrouter/anthropic/claude-sonnet-5                                                      │
│ temperature              │ 1.0                                                                                       │
│ max_output_tokens        │ 16384                                                                                     │
│ diff_summary             │ added: 0; deleted: 0; modified: 16;                                                       │
