│ patch_description        │ The best-performing prior variant (score 0.65) used only 7 distinct parameters by         │
│                          │ splitting the 8 qubits into two halves (0-3 and 4-7) for all single-qubit rotation        │
│                          │ layers, while the current program (score 0.62) uses four quarter-groups (13 distinct      │
│                          │ params). Since parameter economy is scored as strictly beneficial and the two-half split  │
│                          │ already demonstrated superior score with a CRZ-based entangler, we apply the same         │
│                          │ two-half grouping to the current ZZ-ring-based ansatz. This reduces distinct parameters   │
│                          │ from 13 to 7 while preserving the ring ZZ-entangling structure, testing whether the ZZ    │
│                          │ entangler combined with fewer parameters yields even better robustness/margin performance │
│                          │ than the CRZ variant.                                                                     │
