│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ The historical trend across generations shows that reducing the number of distinct        │
│                          │ trainable parameters consistently increases the combined score (18→8 params scored 0.61,  │
│                          │ 10 params scored 0.65, and the current 5-param version scores 0.69, the best so far).     │
│                          │ This suggests the parameter-economy term dominates and the circuit still has enough       │
│                          │ expressivity to fit the small training set even with fewer parameters. Building on this   │
│                          │ trend, I propose merging the two RY pre-rotation parameters (`ry_a`, `ry_b`) into a       │
│                          │ single shared parameter `ry_all` applied to all 8 qubits. This reduces the distinct       │
│                          │ parameter count from 5 to 4, likely improving parameter_efficiency and the combined score │
│                          │ further while the entangling ZZ ring and shared RZ layers preserve enough non-trivial     │
│                          │ correlations to maintain accuracy and margins.                                            │
