│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Based on the top-performing seed structure (RY + RZ pre/post layers with a fully-shared   │
│                          │ ZZ entangling ring, 5 distinct params, score 0.69), I replace the current CZ+CRZ design   │
│                          │ (which scored lower at 0.65 with 7 distinct params) with the proven ZZ-ring structure,    │
│                          │ then apply the recommended refinement: split the single shared "zz_ring" parameter into   │
│                          │ two shared parameters, "zz_even" and "zz_odd", assigned to alternating edges of the ring. │
│                          │ This keeps the same ring topology and gate count while giving the entangling layer two    │
│                          │ degrees of freedom instead of one, potentially improving the worst-group margin without   │
│                          │ significantly hurting parameter economy (6 distinct params total, still very economical). │
│                          │ Removing the extra CZ/CRZ layers also reduces gate count and depth relative to the        │
│                          │ current underperforming variant, which should help convergence speed and reduce the       │
│                          │ train-test gap.                                                                           │
