│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two best-performing seed variants (both scoring 0.69 with 5 distinct     │
│                          │ params). Both showed that duplicating the sandwich block inside the spec (doubling        │
│                          │ depth/gate-count) gives identical score to the single-block version, confirming that raw  │
│                          │ depth/gate-count don't matter much here and that the backend's own repetition mechanism   │
│                          │ already provides the necessary expressivity. Since parameter economy is rewarded "at      │
│                          │ every count", this version keeps the proven sandwich motif (RY pre-rotation -> RZ         │
│                          │ pre-entangle -> ZZ ring -> RZ post-entangle) but pushes parameter sharing further: the    │
│                          │ two RZ groups (rz_a/rz_b) used in the top scorer are merged into a single fully-shared    │
│                          │ "rz" parameter, cutting distinct parameters from 5 down to 4. The RY split into two       │
│                          │ groups (ry_a/ry_b) is kept, since it is the part most likely tied to different halves of  │
│                          │ the (unknown) data encoding and dropping it entirely is a bigger structural risk. The ZZ  │
│                          │ ring is also closed into a full 8-edge ring (adding the wrap-around edge 7-0) at no extra │
│                          │ parameter cost, to strengthen entangling connectivity/robustness for the hardest          │
│                          │ validation groups without touching the parameter budget. Only a single, non-duplicated    │
│                          │ instance of the block is kept (depth ~20-ish) since duplicating didn't change score but   │
│                          │ did increase depth/gate-count, which is never beneficial when scores tie.                 │
