│ patch_description        │ The current candidate underperforms the earlier seed (0.67 vs 0.70) mainly because of the │
│                          │ extra "rz_global" fine-tuning layer, which added a 6th distinct parameter without         │
│                          │ improving margins (worst_group_margin stayed the same while convergence doubled).         │
│                          │ Following the recommendation, I replace this weak addition with an orthogonal-interaction │
│                          │ structure: insert a shared XX ring immediately after the existing ZZ ring (same neighbor  │
│                          │ topology, single shared parameter "xx_ring"), then drop the ineffective global RZ layer.  │
│                          │ Mixing ZZ and XX Ising couplings gives the entangling block access to a richer,           │
│                          │ non-commuting interaction structure that should better separate hard groups (improving    │
│                          │ worst-case margin) while keeping the parameter count unchanged (6 distinct params, same   │
│                          │ as before) and actually reducing gate redundancy compared to the failed global-RZ         │
│                          │ variant.                                                                                  │
