│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ consolidate_rz_shared_with_xx_ring                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ The two seed variants show that reducing distinct parameter count consistently raises the │
│                          │ combined score (best score 0.70 came from the 4-distinct-param design that merged the RZ  │
│                          │ pre/post layers into a single shared "rz_p" parameter, versus 0.67 for the current        │
│                          │ 6-param XX+ZZ design). To combine the benefit of the orthogonal XX/ZZ Ising mixing        │
│                          │ (recommended for margin robustness) with the parameter economy that empirically wins, I   │
│                          │ merge the split rz_a/rz_b pre/post-entangling rotation layers into one fully shared       │
│                          │ "rz_p" parameter (applied to all 8 qubits, before and after the entangling rings), while  │
│                          │ keeping the ZZ ring followed by an XX ring for richer entangling structure. This drops    │
│                          │ distinct parameter count from 6 to 5 (ry_a, ry_b, rz_p, zz_ring, xx_ring), which should   │
│                          │ both increase parameter_efficiency and combined_score, and likely reduce convergence      │
│                          │ steps back toward the 30-step regime seen in the best seed.                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0542                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
