│                          │ sublayers (zz_even on edges 0-1,2-3,4-5,6-7 and zz_odd on edges 1-2,3-4,5-6,7-0) to       │
│                          │ enrich ring expressivity along even vs odd bonds. To keep the total distinct-parameter    │
│                          │ count unchanged at 4 (preserving the parameter-economy advantage that drove the best      │
│                          │ prior score), the two RY pre-rotation groups (ry_a/ry_b) are merged into a single shared  │
│                          │ "ry" parameter, since group-specific RY expressiveness contributed less than the          │
│                          │ entangling-ring structure to the observed margins. The RZ pre/post layers keep sharing    │
│                          │ one fully-shared "rz" parameter as in the best-scoring seed, and a full closed 8-edge     │
│                          │ ring (with wrap-around 7-0) is retained for full connectivity. This design targets a      │
│                          │ robustness improvement on the worst-group margin (via more flexible entangling structure) │
│                          │ without paying the parameter-count penalty seen when moving to 6 distinct params in the   │
│                          │ immediately preceding candidate.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Rationale from the metric history:                                                        │
│                          │ - Best score (0.70) achieved with 4 distinct params, ry_a/ry_b split, shared rz, single   │
│                          │ zz_ring — worst_group_margin 0.36, val_margin 0.73.                                       │
│                          │ - Adding rz_a/rz_b split + xx_ring on top (6 distinct params) dropped score to 0.67       │
│                          │ despite identical accuracy and margin, confirming parameter economy dominates when margin │
│                          │ doesn't improve.                                                                          │
│                          │ - Therefore any added parameter (e.g., splitting zz_ring into zz_even/zz_odd) must be     │
│                          │ offset by removing an existing distinct parameter elsewhere (merging ry_a/ry_b) to avoid  │
│                          │ the same penalty, while still testing the entangling-ring flexibility recommendation.     │
