│ patch_description        │ The best-performing seed (score 0.71, 4 distinct params) used an RY pre-rotation layer    │
│                          │ split into wires 0-3 vs 4-7, followed by a fixed CNOT ladder, a shared global RZ phase, a │
│                          │ parametrized ZZ entangling ring (with long-range cross couplings sharing the same         │
│                          │ parameter), a backward CNOT ladder, and a repeated RZ phase. The current program (0.69)   │
│                          │ diverged from this structure by adding an extra RZ pair of parameters and orthogonal XX   │
│                          │ gates, which increased parameter count and reduced score.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This edit restores the higher-scoring seed-1 structure (4 distinct params: ry_a, ry_b,    │
│                          │ rz_p, zz_ring) but tests the recommended alternate partition for the RY layer: even wires │
│                          │ [0,2,4,6] share "ry_a" and odd wires [1,3,5,7] share "ry_b", instead of the contiguous    │
│                          │ 0-3/4-7 split. This preserves the exact parameter economy and topology that achieved      │
│                          │ perfect train/val/test accuracy while exploring whether an interleaved qubit grouping     │
│                          │ (which pairs more naturally with the alternating CNOT ladder and ring couplings) can      │
│                          │ improve the worst-group margin — the dominant term in the combined score — without        │
│                          │ changing param count.                                                                     │
