│ patch_description        │ Duplicate the entire RY→CNOT→RZ→ZZ(ring+cross)→CNOT→RZ sequence as a second block         │
│                          │ appended after the first, reusing all four existing parameter names (ry_a, ry_b, rz_p,    │
│                          │ zz_ring) so n_distinct_params stays at 4. In the second block, replace the long-range     │
│                          │ cross-coupling pattern ([0,4],[1,5],[2,6],[3,7]) with the complementary diagonal set      │
│                          │ ([0,5],[1,6],[2,7],[3,4]), giving the circuit richer non-local entanglement coverage      │
│                          │ across both diagonal directions of the qubit register. This increases expressive power    │
│                          │ and connectivity (helping separate the worst-margin group) while keeping the parameter    │
│                          │ count fixed, following the proven "sandwich" motif that previously improved margins       │
│                          │ without harming convergence speed.                                                        │
