│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ zz_nn_lr_split                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the even/odd ZZ ring split with a physically motivated distinction between        │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor ring couplings and long-range cross-link couplings. All 8 ring edges     │
│                          │ (0-1,1-2,...,7-0) share a single "zz_nn" parameter, and 4 diagonal cross-links            │
│                          │ (0-4,1-5,2-6,3-7) share a single "zz_lr" parameter. This keeps the same 4 distinct        │
│                          │ trainable parameter names (ry, rz, zz_nn, zz_lr) but gives the optimizer independent      │
│                          │ control over local adjacency structure versus long-range entanglement, which should       │
│                          │ improve the worst-group margin (as previously observed with the full ring + cross-link    │
│                          │ seed scoring 0.71) while retaining the shallower/parameter-economic circuit style of the  │
│                          │ current best variant.                                                                     │
