│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ hybrid_ladder_shared_ry                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the previous 4-parameter variant, this version pushes parameter economy       │
│                          │ further by merging the two RY pre-rotation groups into a single shared parameter          │
│                          │ (`ry_p`), reducing distinct trainable parameters from 4 to 3 while preserving full        │
│                          │ 8-qubit RY coverage. It also applies the recommended CNOT/CZ hybridization: every third   │
│                          │ gate in both the forward and backward entangling ladders (on wire-pairs [2,3]/[5,6]       │
│                          │ forward and [5,4]/[2,1] backward) is replaced with a CZ gate. This diversifies the        │
│                          │ entangling structure (mixing CNOT's directional propagation with CZ's symmetric           │
│                          │ phase-kick) at zero additional parameter cost, which prior insight suggests accelerates   │
│                          │ convergence and deepens correlation mixing — directly helping the worst-group margin and  │
│                          │ reducing convergence steps. The shared global RZ phase and the ring+long-range ZZ         │
│                          │ coupling (still tied to one shared `zz_ring` parameter) are kept unchanged since they     │
│                          │ already contribute strongly to the entangling ring driving perfect train/val/test         │
│                          │ accuracy. Overall this keeps circuit depth and gate count essentially identical while     │
│                          │ trimming parameter count for a higher parameter-economy score without sacrificing the     │
│                          │ already-perfect accuracy metrics.                                                         │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0529                                                                                   │
