│ patch_description        │ The long-range hypercube couplings ([0,4],[1,5],[2,6],[3,7]) currently share the same     │
│                          │ "zz_ring" parameter as the nearest-neighbor ring, which may limit the optimizer's ability │
│                          │ to independently tune short-range vs. long-range entanglement strength. Splitting these   │
│                          │ primary diagonals into their own shared parameter "zz_lr" (distinct from zz_ring but      │
│                          │ still a single shared name across all 4 gates) gives the optimizer one extra degree of    │
│                          │ freedom to balance local vs. global correlations, which should help separate              │
│                          │ harder-to-classify samples that depend on longer-range qubit correlations, improving      │
│                          │ worst-group margin at the cost of only one additional parameter (5 distinct params total  │
│                          │ instead of 4).                                                                            │
