│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_zz_add_xx_ring                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce parameter count further and boost expressivity at zero extra parameter cost by     │
│                          │ merging the previous "zz_even"/"zz_odd" split into a single fully-shared "zz_ring"        │
│                          │ parameter (dropping distinct params from 4 to 3, matching the best-scoring prior seed),   │
│                          │ and by adding a complementary XX nearest-neighbor ring reusing the same "zz_ring"         │
│                          │ parameter name right after the ZZ ring. Mixing ZZ (diagonal) and XX (off-diagonal)        │
│                          │ two-qubit interactions on the same ring topology increases the entangling power /         │
│                          │ expressivity of the ansatz without adding any new trainable parameter, which prior        │
│                          │ evidence suggests improves worst-group margin robustness. This keeps total distinct       │
│                          │ parameters at 3 (ry, rz, zz_ring), which should improve parameter_efficiency and the      │
│                          │ combined score similar to (or better than) the earlier 0.72-scoring seed.                 │
