│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ merge_ry_and_add_xx_ring                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Two combined improvements based on the best-performing prior variant (score 0.72) and the │
│                          │ explicit recommendation:                                                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Merge the two RY groups (`ry_a`, `ry_b`) into a single shared `ry_a` parameter across  │
│                          │ all 8 qubits. This cuts the distinct parameter count from 4 to 3, which the scoring       │
│                          │ function rewards strongly (parameter economy is always beneficial), while the entangling  │
│                          │ structure still provides enough expressivity to separate classes.                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. Immediately after the ZZ ring layer, add an XX ring (nearest-neighbor, wrapping 7-0)   │
│                          │ reusing the same `zz_ring` parameter name. Mixing ZZ and XX terms on the same coupling    │
│                          │ parameter gives the entangling layer access to non-commuting two-qubit interactions       │
│                          │ (complementary Ising axes), which has been shown to improve expressivity and robustness   │
│                          │ of the worst-margin group without any additional trainable parameters.                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Together these changes reduce n_distinct_params from 4 to 3 while enriching the           │
│                          │ entangling layer's expressivity, which should improve both parameter_efficiency and       │
│                          │ worst_group_margin.                                                                       │
