│ patch_name               │ add_extended_zz_connectivity                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ The current candidate uses only a nearest-neighbor ZZ ring (8 edges) for entangling,      │
│                          │ while the higher-scoring prior seed (score 0.72) enriched connectivity with additional    │
│                          │ "opposite-qubit" and "skip-2" ZZ couplings, all sharing the same `zz_ring` parameter name │
│                          │ (so no new trainable parameters are introduced). This extra connectivity gives the ansatz │
│                          │ more expressive power to separate the hardest validation group (worst_group_margin)       │
│                          │ without any parameter-count penalty, at the cost of a modest depth increase. I apply the  │
│                          │ same idea here: after the nearest-neighbor ring, add the opposite-qubit couplings (i,     │
│                          │ i+4) and the skip-2 shell (i, i+2 mod 8), all still under the shared `zz_ring` parameter. │
│                          │ This mirrors the recommendation to clone/deepen the entangling block while keeping the    │
│                          │ parameter economy intact.                                                                 │
