│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ none                                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Crossover of the two highest-scoring seeds. From the 0.72-scoring seed we keep the        │
│                          │ fully-shared RY pre-rotation layer (single "ry_a" parameter across all 8 qubits) and the  │
│                          │ enriched entangling topology (nearest-neighbor ring + opposite-qubit long-range links +   │
│                          │ skip-2 shell, all Ising ZZ couplers). From the 0.71-scoring seed we keep the sandwich     │
│                          │ structure of global RZ phase layers around the entangling block and the forward/backward  │
│                          │ CNOT ladders that provide extra zero-parameter mixing.                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The key new idea driving this crossover is parameter unification across gate types: both  │
│                          │ the RZ phase layers and all ZZ couplers reuse the SAME trainable parameter name           │
│                          │ ("theta"), which is allowed since parameter sharing is defined purely by string identity, │
│                          │ not gate type. This collapses the previous 3-distinct-parameter design (ry_a, rz_p,       │
│                          │ zz_ring) down to just 2 distinct parameters (ry_a, theta) while preserving the full       │
│                          │ expressive gate structure (same depth/gate-count as the strongest seed). Since the        │
│                          │ scoring rule states parameter economy always dominates with no diminishing returns,       │
│                          │ cutting from 3 to 2 distinct parameters should directly improve the score, provided the   │
│                          │ rich connectivity (ring + long-range + skip-2, sandwiched with RZ phase layers and        │
│                          │ bidirectional CNOT ladders) preserves the robust separation and worst-group margin        │
│                          │ observed in the top-performing seeds.                                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0620                                                                                   │
│ error_attempt            │ None                                                                                      │
