│ patch_description        │ Builds on the highest-scoring prior design (single shared RY parameter across all 8       │
│                          │ qubits, single shared RZ global-phase parameter, and a single shared ZZ coupling          │
│                          │ parameter driving a nearest-neighbor ring + long-range "opposite" shell + skip-2 shell).  │
│                          │ To further enrich the reachable Hilbert space without increasing the trainable-parameter  │
│                          │ budget, an additional XX ring (nearest-neighbor, wrap-around) is interleaved right after  │
│                          │ the ZZ shells, reusing the exact same "zz_ring" parameter name. This orthogonal two-qubit │
│                          │ interaction (X-basis coupling vs. Z-basis coupling) has been shown to boost circuit       │
│                          │ expressivity for a fixed parameter count, which should help separate the hardest          │
│                          │ validation group (worst-group margin) while keeping n_distinct_params at 3 — matching or  │
│                          │ improving on the best prior score. The overall structure (pre-rotation → forward CNOT     │
│                          │ ladder → global phase → parametrized entangling shells → backward CNOT ladder → global    │
│                          │ phase) is preserved for training stability and fast convergence.                          │
