│ patch_description        │ Two coordinated changes to push toward the higher-scoring 3-distinct-parameter regime     │
│                          │ while deepening the entangling structure (per the recommendation to repeat the ZZ block   │
│                          │ under a shared parameter):                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Merge the `ry_a`/`ry_b` split into a single shared `ry_a` parameter across all 8       │
│                          │ qubits, reducing distinct trainable parameters from 4 to 3 (matching the configuration    │
│                          │ that previously scored 0.72, which strongly rewards parameter economy).                   │
│                          │ 2. Add a "skip-2" connectivity shell (0-2,1-3,2-4,3-5,4-6,5-7,6-0,7-1) and then repeat    │
│                          │ the entire three-shell ZZ block (ring + opposite + skip-2) a second time, all reusing the │
│                          │ single `zz_ring` parameter. This increases entangling depth/expressivity at zero extra    │
│                          │ parameter cost, which the notes indicate previously yielded a modest score lift, aiming   │
│                          │ to better separate the hardest validation group (worst-group margin) while keeping        │
│                          │ n_distinct_params at 3.                                                                   │
