│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ theta_shared_zz_yy_skip2_shell                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the best-performing 2-distinct-parameter structure (ry_a + theta) from the      │
│                          │ prior 0.73-scoring seed, and apply the recommended enhancement: add a YY entangling shell │
│                          │ on the same skip-2 qubit pairs as the ZZ skip-2 shell, all sharing the single "theta"     │
│                          │ parameter. This injects Y-basis coupling orthogonal to the existing Z-basis coupling,     │
│                          │ densifying the reachable unitary set without adding any new trainable parameters (still   │
│                          │ only 2 distinct param names: ry_a, theta), which should improve worst-group               │
│                          │ margin/separation while preserving the excellent parameter economy that drove the 0.73    │
│                          │ score. The previous 6-parameter variant (zz_even/zz_odd/rz_a/rz_b) scored lower (0.67),   │
│                          │ confirming that reducing distinct parameter count and increasing shared entangling        │
│                          │ structure is the more promising direction.                                                │
