│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_yy_skip2_shell_shared_param                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Following the recommendation to complement the ZZ entangling shells with orthogonal       │
│                          │ Y-basis coupling, I add a YY entangling shell on the same skip-2 qubit pairs              │
│                          │ ([0,2],[1,3],[2,4],[3,5],[4,6],[5,7],[6,0],[7,1]) immediately after the existing ZZ       │
│                          │ skip-2 shell. Crucially, this reuses the SAME shared parameter name "zz_ring" already     │
│                          │ used for all ZZ couplings, so no new trainable parameter is introduced (n_distinct_params │
│                          │ stays at 4). Adding YY interactions in addition to ZZ on the same connectivity pattern    │
│                          │ increases the reachable entangled state space (since [XX,YY,ZZ] generators don't          │
│                          │ commute), which should help the circuit separate harder validation groups without any     │
│                          │ parameter-count penalty, echoing the successful ZZ-density strategy from prior            │
│                          │ high-scoring seeds but adding a complementary rotation axis.                              │
