│ patch_description        │ Merge all trainable parameters into a single shared name "theta" (following the           │
│                          │ highest-scoring prior seed which used only 2 distinct params and scored 0.73, confirming  │
│                          │ parameter economy dominates the score). This drops distinct parameter count from 4 to 1,  │
│                          │ which per the scoring rules should improve combined_score directly through                │
│                          │ parameter_efficiency and likely also tightens generalization since fewer free parameters  │
│                          │ restrict overfitting on the small training set. Additionally, append a second             │
│                          │ zero-parameter CNOT mixing ladder (forward 0→7 then backward 7→0) after the final RZ      │
│                          │ layer, as recommended, to further mix qubit correlations and break residual correlations  │
│                          │ without touching the parameter budget. This combines the two most successful zero-cost    │
│                          │ levers seen across prior generations: aggressive parameter sharing and deeper fixed-gate  │
│                          │ mixing.                                                                                   │
