│ patch_name               │ duplicate_zz_shell_zzring                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Building on the current program's shared "zz_ring" parameter (used across the ring,       │
│                          │ opposite-qubit, and skip-2 ZZ shells, plus the orthogonal YY skip-2 shell), I replicate   │
│                          │ the ZZ ring + opposite-qubit + skip-2 shell sequence a second time immediately after the  │
│                          │ first occurrence, still exclusively using param="zz_ring". This adds additional           │
│                          │ entangling depth (a second "shell" of the same connectivity pattern) without introducing  │
│                          │ any new trainable parameter name, which is the dominant lever for score since fewer       │
│                          │ distinct parameters always scores higher. Extra depth under a shared parameter increases  │
│                          │ the effective nonlinearity of the feature map, which should help widen the margin on the  │
│                          │ hardest validation group (worst_group_margin) while keeping n_distinct_params unchanged.  │
