│ patch_description        │ The current candidate uses 4 distinct trainable parameters (ry_a, ry_b, rz, zz_ring) and  │
│                          │ scored 0.70, while the earlier 2-parameter seed (ry_a shared across all qubits, theta     │
│                          │ shared across RZ+ZZ layers) scored 0.73 with better parameter economy and                 │
│                          │ comparable/better margins. Since parameter economy is weighted very heavily in the score  │
│                          │ (fewer distinct params always scores higher, no diminishing returns), I revert to the     │
│                          │ proven 2-parameter structure (single ry_a pre-rotation, single theta driving RZ layers    │
│                          │ and all ZZ entangling shells) and extend it with the recommended skip-3 ZZ coupling shell │
│                          │ (pairs at hypercube distance 3: [0,3],[1,4],[2,5],[3,6],[4,7],[5,0],[6,1],[7,2]), still   │
│                          │ reusing "theta". This densifies entanglement connectivity further (potentially improving  │
│                          │ the worst-group margin, which dominates the score) without adding any new trainable       │
│                          │ parameter, combining the best of both prior seeds' strengths.                             │
