│ patch_description        │ Revert to the 2-distinct-parameter structure that scored best (0.74), where a single      │
│                          │ "ry_a" drives all RY pre-rotations and a single "theta" drives every RZ/ZZ/XX coupling.   │
│                          │ On top of that proven backbone, add one more zero-new-parameter entangling shell: a       │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor YY ring (wires 0-1,...,7-0) that reuses "theta". Adding an orthogonal    │
│                          │ Y-basis coupling alongside the existing Z-basis (ZZ) and X-basis (XX) couplings further   │
│                          │ enriches the accessible operator algebra (approaching a fuller SU(2)xSU(2) mixing per     │
│                          │ edge), which should help increase the worst-group margin (the dominant score term)        │
│                          │ without increasing the parameter count, since the previous XX-ring addition alone already │
│                          │ improved score from 0.73 to 0.74. This keeps n_distinct_params = 2, preserving the        │
│                          │ parameter-economy advantage while pushing the robust-separation term higher.              │
