│ patch_name               │ dual_shell_shared_theta_revert                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The 4-distinct-parameter version (ry_a/ry_b/rz/zz_ring) scored lower (0.70) than the      │
│                          │ earlier 2-distinct-parameter design (0.74) despite similar accuracy, because parameter    │
│                          │ economy and convergence speed dominate the score. This edit reverts to the proven         │
│                          │ 2-parameter structure (single shared "ry_a" pre-rotation and single shared "theta"        │
│                          │ driving all RZ/ZZ/XX couplers), and applies the recommended duplication: the entire       │
│                          │ parametrized multi-shell block (ZZ ring, ZZ opposite-qubit, ZZ skip-2, XX ring) is        │
│                          │ duplicated once more under the same "theta" parameter, placed right before the backward   │
│                          │ CNOT ladder. This increases expressivity per parameter (evidence: prior duplication       │
│                          │ lifted score 0.71->0.73) while keeping n_distinct_params at 2, which should improve       │
│                          │ robustness/worst-group margin without any parameter-count penalty.                        │
