│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_cry_skip2_shell                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a CRY skip-2 shell immediately after the existing XX ring block, reusing the shared   │
│                          │ "theta" parameter. This introduces controlled-Y rotations across skip-2 connectivity (i   │
│                          │ -> i+2 mod 8), broadening the operator basis beyond the current Ising XX/ZZ couplings     │
│                          │ without adding any new trainable parameter name. Controlled rotations (CRY) are           │
│                          │ qualitatively different from the Ising-type ZZ/XX couplings already present (they are not │
│                          │ simply exponentials of a fixed Pauli tensor product but asymmetric controlled             │
│                          │ operations), so mixing them in should increase expressivity/entangling variety useful for │
│                          │ separating the hardest validation group, while keeping n_distinct_params at 2.            │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
