                         Patch Metadata - Gen 78/80 - Novelty: 1/2 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 2/2                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ single_theta_with_mid_rz_sandwich                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ Revert to the previously best-performing single-shared-parameter design                   │
│                          │ (n_distinct_params=1, which scored 0.77 vs the current 5-parameter version's 0.69) and    │
│                          │ apply the recommended enhancement: insert a mid-block global RZ layer (reusing the same   │
│                          │ shared "theta" parameter) sandwiched between the ZZ/XX entangling rings and the backward  │
│                          │ CNOT ladder. This creates a triple RZ sandwich (pre-entangling, mid, post-entangling)     │
│                          │ around the entangling shells, deepening phase-correlation structure while keeping the     │
│                          │ parameter count at the theoretical minimum of 1 distinct trainable parameter. Since       │
│                          │ parameter economy dominates scoring and the single-theta topology already generalized     │
│                          │ well (worst_group_margin 0.35, validation_margin 0.70), adding the extra RZ layer without │
│                          │ new parameters should further improve robust separation without any generalization cost.  │
